https://ollama.com/blog/mlx

=C2=A0
Today, we're previewing the fastest =
way to run Ollama on Apple silicon, powered by MLX, Apple's machine =
learning framework.
=C2=A0
This change accelerates your most demanding work=
 on macOS:


 * Personal assistants like OpenClaw

 * Coding agents like =
Claude Code, OpenCode, or Codex



Fastest performance on Apple silicon, =
powered by MLX

Ollama on Apple silicon is now built on top of =
Apple=E2=80=99s machine learning framework, MLX, to take advantage of its =
unified memory
architecture.
=C2=A0
This results in a large speedup of =
Ollama on all Apple Silicon devices. On Apple=E2=80=99s M5, M5 Pro and M5 =
Max chips, Ollama leverages
the new GPU Neural Accelerators to accelerate =
both time to first token (TTFT) and generation speed (tokens per second).
=C2=A0



Testing was conducted using Alibaba=E2=80=99s Qwen3.5-35B-A3B =
model quantized to NVFP4 and Ollama=E2=80=99s previous implementation =
quantized to Q4_K_M using Ollama 0.18. Ollama 0.19 will see even higher =
performance (1851 token/s prefill and 134 token/s decode) when running =
withint4 quantization



NVFP4 support: higher quality responses and =
production parity

Ollama now leverages NVIDIA=E2=80=99s NVFP4
[https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/introducing-nvfp4-for-efficient-and-accu=
rate-low-precision-inference/] format to maintain model
accuracy while reducing memory bandwidth and storage requirements for =
inference workloads.
=C2=A0
As more inference providers scale inference =
using NVFP4 format, this allows Ollama users to share the same results as =
they would
in a production environment.
=C2=A0
It further opens up Ollama =
to have the ability to run models optimized by NVIDIA=E2=80=99s model =
optimizer
[https://github.com/NVIDIA/Model-Optimizer]. Other precisions =
will be made available based on the design and usage intent from
Ollama=E2=80=99s research and hardware partners.
=C2=A0


Improved caching for more responsiveness

Ollama=E2=80=99s cache has been =
upgraded to make coding and agentic tasks more efficient.


 * Lower memory utilization: Ollama will now reuse its cache across =
conversations, meaning less memory utilization and more cache
   hits when branching when using a shared system prompt with tools like =
Claude Code.
  =20
  =20

 * Intelligent checkpoints: Ollama will now store=
 snapshots of its cache at intelligent locations in the prompt, resulting =
in less
   prompt processing and faster responses.
  =20
  =20

 * Smarter eviction: shared prefixes survive longer even when older =
branches are dropped.

=C2=A0


Get started

Download Ollama =
[https://ollama.com/download]

=C2=A0
This preview release of Ollama =
accelerates the new Qwen3.5-35B-A3B [https://ollama.com/library/qwen3.5] =
model, with sampling
parameters tuned for coding tasks.
=C2=A0
Please make sure you have a Mac with more than 32GB of unified memory.
=C2=A0
Claude Code:
=C2=A0
ollama launch claude --model qwen3.=
5:35b-a3b-coding-nvfp4
=C2=A0
OpenClaw:
=C2=A0
ollama launch openclaw =
--model qwen3.5:35b-a3b-coding-nvfp4
=C2=A0
Chat with the model:
=C2=A0
ollama run qwen3.5:35b-a3b-coding-nvfp4
=C2=A0


Future models

We are actively working to support future models. For users with custom =
models fine-tuned on supported architectures, we will
introduce an easier way to import models into Ollama. In the meantime, we =
will expand the list of supported architectures.
=C2=A0
If you have any feedback, please directly reply to this email or join =
Ollama's Discord channel
[https://discord.com/invite/ollama].
=C2=A0
=E2=9D=A4=EF=B8=8F Ollama
=C2=A0
You are receiving this email because you =
opted-in to receive updates from Ollama
